-- title:
--   Branch ideals at a crossing meet in the ideal (p)
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ with $5 \le p$ and a package $\mathfrak X : \mathrm{DRModelPackage}\ p$, that is, the two-chart integral model $\mathrm{DRModel}\ p$ of the modular curve over $\mathbb Z$ together with the data recorded in that structure (properness, flatness and integrality of the structure morphism $\mathrm{DRModel.toBase}\ p$, integral closedness of the sections over affine opens, the curve models over $\mathbb Q$ and over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with their identifications and Galois compatibilities, the two sections $\varepsilon_\infty,\varepsilon_0$, the smooth locus, and the further components of the package). Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $p$, let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, and let $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa$ be a ring homomorphism. Write $X_O$ for $\mathrm{baseChangeO}\ p\ O$, the base change of the model to $O$. Let $n$ be a point of the fibre product of the two component morphisms $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compInf}\ \kappa$ and $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compZero}\ \kappa$, and let $x_n = \mathfrak X.\mathrm{crossingPt}\ O\ \kappa\ \mathrm{to}\kappa\ n$ be its image in $X_O$ under the first projection followed by $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compInf}\ \kappa$ followed by $\mathrm{DRModel.baseChangeMap}\ \mathrm{to}\kappa$. Assume that the two points $\xi_\infty = \mathfrak X.\xi\mathrm{inf}\ O\ \kappa\ \mathrm{to}\kappa$ and $\xi_0 = \mathfrak X.\xi\mathrm{zero}\ O\ \kappa\ \mathrm{to}\kappa$ both specialise to $x_n$. For such a specialisation $\xi \rightsquigarrow x$, the branch ideal $\mathrm{Scheme.branchIdeal}$ is the preimage of the maximal ideal of the stalk at $\xi$ under the specialisation map $\mathcal O_{X_O,x} \to \mathcal O_{X_O,\xi}$. The assertion is that the intersection of the branch ideals attached to the two specialisations equals the principal ideal of $\mathcal O_{X_O,x_n}$ generated by $\mathrm{baseGerm}\ O\ x_n\ p$, the germ at $x_n$ of the global section of $X_O$ obtained from $p \in O$ along the structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} O$.
--
--   This is the scheme-theoretic statement that near a crossing point of the special fibre of the Deligne–Rapoport model over $O$ the fibre over $(p)$ is the union of the two branches through that point: a germ vanishing on both branches is exactly a multiple of the uniformiser $p$. It feeds the local analysis of crossings, being used in the production of a pair of germs spanning a branch ideal and in the construction of oriented crossing charts.
